findings=[
 {'id':'Q314','title':'Native accessibility bypasses retained scroll correction and reports unscrolled control bounds','source':'crates/cambium/cambium-winit-a11y/src/lib.rs:238; crates/cambium/cambium-rootstock/src/lib.rs:381,439','status':'verified actual current DOM/Host/layout with unchanged extracted native lowering over exact retained suppliers','evidence':'Rootstock document_projection rewrites bounds with OwnedLayout::painted_rect after generic semantic projection. The browser consumes that projection. Native project_tree_with_actions calls genet_render::accesskit_tree_with_style directly with raw fragments and neither scroll offsets nor the Rootstock correction, then scales only the tree root. Two real current Host checks, one viewport and one nested scroll, move a button from y=300 to painted y=150. Neutral bounds correctly report y=150; the exact original native lowering reports y=300 in both cases. A root DPI/zoom transform cannot repair an omitted scroll translation. No OS screen-reader or physical hit testing was executed.','diagnostics':['accessibility_authority_v2_probe_receipt.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Lower the already corrected shared projection, preserving platform-specific producer/leaf semantics and action custody. Add scroll-plane coverage at that shared boundary rather than another independent bounds algorithm.'}},
 {'id':'Q315','title':'Native accessibility still maps and activates a node absent from the published tree','source':'crates/cambium/cambium-winit-a11y/src/lib.rs:179,252; crates/cambium/cambium-rootstock/src/frame.rs:899','status':'verified unchanged native projection and request-mapper functions with real current Host dispatch; no OS action execution','evidence':'project_tree_with_actions walks the entire DOM and inserts every node into action_map before considering whether the style-aware accessibility tree contains it. map_parts checks that map, not current publication or supported actions. In a real current Host, a button is changed to display:none and relaid out: the exact native projection omits the node, but retains its action route. The unchanged original map_parts method, using fixture storage for its two actual maps, returns a Click request, and actual Host::apply_a11y_requests activates the hidden button, incrementing state. Thus the documented refusal for a target no longer in the tree is false. This can affect an action queued before hiding and drained against a later sync; the probe does not claim observed OS queue timing.','diagnostics':['accessibility_authority_v2_probe_receipt.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Build action routes from the current exposed projection and enforce current action eligibility at consumption. Keep textbox/producer pruning consistent; do not treat all retained DOM IDs as current accessibility authority.'}},
 {'id':'Q316','title':'The same custom leaf receives different accessible names on native and browser hosts','source':'crates/cambium/cambium-winit-a11y/src/lib.rs:260; crates/cambium/cambium-genet-web-host/src/mirror.rs:170','status':'verified unchanged native/browser pure lowerings and real current DOM/layout; OS AT and browser DOM application not executed','evidence':'Native projection invokes a sprigging leaf accessibility hook on the existing AccessKit node, so the hook can overwrite an author aria-label. Browser lowering treats ordinary leaf semantics as names_itself=false and explicitly gives the author name precedence. The same custom-leaf with aria-label Author name and a leaf hook naming itself Leaf name projects Leaf name natively, while the exact browser mirror planner retains Author name. Producer-owned slot naming is deliberately distinct, so that exception does not account for this ordinary leaf disagreement. The test uses real current layout and unchanged pure adapters; it does not assert an OS/browser announcement.','diagnostics':['accessibility_authority_v2_probe_receipt.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Choose and publish one ordinary-leaf naming precedence in the shared semantic owner, preserving the separate producer slot policy. Derive both platform outputs from it.'}},
 {'id':'Q317','title':'GPU producer refusal test checks a local image key that the live registry never stages','source':'crates/cambium/cambium-genet-winit-host/tests/checked_producer_refusal.rs:256; crates/cambium/cambium-rootstock/src/producer/registry.rs:31,261,287','status':'source-verified blind assertion; ignored GPU test not executed','evidence':'The test claims a failed producer has already unregistered its previous staged image because unregister_external_image(external_image_key(KEY)) returns false. KEY is the local registry key 807. Current ProducerRegistry allocates an unrelated process-wide physical key in the upper half of the lower-62-bit domain and stages/retire by that allocated key; image_identity exposes it. For local 807, external_image_key(KEY) is consequently not the staged binding. This assertion returns false for an absent unrelated key even if the actual physical image were still live, so it cannot prove the claimed invalidation. The rest of the test has separate typed failure/authority checks, which are not invalidated by this one blind check.','repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Capture the actual pre-refusal ProducerImageIdentity::renderer_key, establish that binding exists in a positive control, and assert its retirement. Do not apply external_image_key again to the full returned renderer key.'}},
 {'id':'Q318','title':'Headed device-reuse negative controls clear the cache while leaving the device authority intact','source':'crates/cambium/cambium-genet-winit-host/src/headed_tests.rs:90,492,663; crates/cambium/cambium-genet-winit-host/src/lib.rs:460','status':'source-verified stale control perturbation; headed tests not rerun','evidence':'The one-window control and the multi-window third-window control expect clearing shared.render_core to force a second device boot. Current native render_core first consults shared.render_recovery, reattaches that owner and returns owner.current; the owner is installed on first boot and is not cleared by either control. Resume also polls the same recovery owner. Both purported forget-the-device perturbations therefore leave the actual authority available and no longer exercise the old two-device behavior they claim to detect. The assertions expect a second boot, so this is an obsolete negative control, not a claim that those ignored tests currently pass.','repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Construct an explicit isolated negative-control ownership graph and verify its distinct device identity. Keep the ordinary shared-recovery path intact; a cached Arc is no longer the device owner.'}},
 {'id':'Q319','title':'Windows multi-window idle policy can poll continuously for a minimized window it refuses to draw','source':'crates/cambium/cambium-genet-winit-host/src/windows.rs:377,398,416','status':'source-verified scheduling predicate mismatch; native minimize/CPU runtime not executed','evidence':'The Windows about_to_wait draw loop considers a window showing only when it is not app-hidden and its native window is not minimized. A minimized window therefore skips asked(), leaving its paced wanted flag set. The later owed predicate checks only !hidden and wanted.get(), omitting the minimized check, and selects ControlFlow::Poll when true. A minimized, otherwise nonhidden window with a pending redraw thus continuously requests idle turns while the same code declines to consume its request. The Minimize command changes native state without setting app-hidden, so those are distinct states in the shipping wrapper. This is the exact boolean counterexample, not an observed OS CPU measurement.','repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Use one eligible-to-draw predicate when drawing and deciding whether to poll, preserving the owed redraw for restoration and the normal monitor-paced path.'}}
]
