rows=[
 ('Shared generic semantics do not imply one final projection','Native and browser share the supplier semantic base, then apply separate Mere postprocessing.', ['crates/cambium/cambium-winit-a11y/src/lib.rs','crates/cambium/cambium-rootstock/src/lib.rs','crates/cambium/cambium-genet-web-host/src/mirror.rs'], 'The inspected cached supplier accesskit_tree_with_style lowers document_a11y_projection_with_style, so it is not an independently invented generic ARIA engine. Q314/Q316 are the actual divergence: retained scroll correction and ordinary leaf naming after that base. The inspected supplier source is hashed separately; fresh whole supplier compilation is not claimed.'),
 ('Accessibility target custody is a second stateful authority','Native action maps include DOM nodes not necessarily in the published tree.', ['crates/cambium/cambium-winit-a11y/src/lib.rs','crates/cambium/cambium-rootstock/src/frame.rs'], 'Q315 proves a hidden target remains mappable and activates through actual Host dispatch. The public raw-request mapper also discards target_tree, as does sync mapping of bridge requests; composition experiments deliberately use a separate tree-qualified GraftTable. Do not claim the ordinary A11yHost implements the experiment tree-routing seam.'),
 ('App textbox pruning is duplicated after shared semantics','Both Rootstock neutral projection and native AccessKit cleanup make marked app fields into committed-value leaves.', ['crates/cambium/cambium-winit-a11y/src/lib.rs','crates/cambium/cambium-rootstock/src/lib.rs'], 'Native code maintains its own descendant removal, focus fallback and action/producer-map pruning. Current source tests cover nested marked fields and preserve drawing DOM. They were read, not rerun as complete original adapter tests. A shared generic base does not eliminate these repeated owner rules.'),
 ('Producer accessibility IDs are two copies of the same recipe','Native produced_node_id and browser drawn_id independently hash slot, child and optional action into the high-bit domain.', ['crates/cambium/cambium-winit-a11y/src/lib.rs','crates/cambium/cambium-genet-web-host/src/mirror.rs'], 'Current formulas agree by source trace; no ID mismatch is claimed. Role conversion, child/button bounds, naming and action-map construction remain separately implemented. Track this unshared ABI recipe even where current behavior matches.'),
 ('Installation state records an attempted install as installed','A11yHost sets installed=true after either outcome from bridge.install.', ['crates/cambium/cambium-winit-a11y/src/lib.rs'], 'The failure is logged and bridge.status remains separately queryable; later sync calls update instead of retrying install. Source alone does not establish platform retry capability or a newly observed outage. Keep this as a named success/state follow-up instead of claiming every logged failure is silently successful.'),
 ('Native receipt controls lag actual resource custody','The GPU refusal and headed reuse tests probe identifiers/caches that no longer name the owned resource.', ['crates/cambium/cambium-genet-winit-host/tests/checked_producer_refusal.rs','crates/cambium/cambium-genet-winit-host/src/headed_tests.rs'], 'Q317 identifies a blind local-key unregistration assertion; Q318 identifies cache-only negative controls retaining the recovery owner. These source facts do not become new GPU/native pass receipts. Ordinary tests explicitly mark actual device/headed gates ignored and serialized.'),
 ('Multi-window scheduling has a platform-local eligibility fork','Paced redraw custody is shared through wanted flags, but Windows draw admission and poll admission differ.', ['crates/cambium/cambium-genet-winit-host/src/windows.rs'], 'Q319 records the minimized-window spin counterexample. Other platform code hands paced requests to native delivery instead. Recovery polls every window including hidden hosts before first-window-only application wake hooks, with a bounded CPU recovery test in source.'),
 ('Published winit translation and full native host repeat keyboard mapping','The thin adapter emits runner KeyEvent, while the full host converts the same winit names into Rootstock KeyPress.', ['crates/cambium/cambium-winit/src/lib.rs','crates/cambium/cambium-genet-winit-host/src/lib.rs'], 'Both spell named-key and modifier conversion separately. The thin adapter drops unidentified keys because its API lacks injected event text; full host preserves injected text via KeyPress. composition_from_winit and ime_event_from_winit themselves duplicate the same IME match. Record bounded compatibility versus current routing rather than claiming one shared implementation.'),
 ('Shared scrollbar policy has an unimplemented retained paint endpoint','ScrollbarFade owns hold/fade state and wheel_axes maps Shift gestures; Rootstock calls it but its append_scrollbars remains empty.', ['crates/cambium/cambium-winit/src/scroll.rs','crates/cambium/cambium-rootstock/src/owned_layout.rs'], 'This joins the earlier retained-stub follow-up with its actual reusable clock. Fade values are fixed constants and may keep redraws alive despite the empty wrapper paint endpoint. Do not claim absence across every independent supplier paint route without tracing it.'),
 ('Composition experiments qualify multiple consumers but retain separate orchestration','E1a/E1b construct real sessions and explicit tree graft routing alongside the standard adapter.', ['crates/cambium/cambium-winit-a11y/tests/e1a_sessions.rs','crates/cambium/cambium-winit-a11y/examples/e1b_two_sessions.rs'], 'E1a source runs six cases against three pinned accesskit consumers and distinguishes process-wide DOM IDs from cross-source ID collisions. E1b owns a standalone adapter, activation tree, queue, focus order, manual typing and caret-area publication; panes are not painted. Its self-check prints observations rather than asserting the manual OS walk. Source read is not consumer/native AT execution.'),
 ('Native integration tests support narrow claims, not blanket acceptance','The completed suite source covers scroll, caret, layout, semantics, capture refusal/pairing, lifecycle and reflow.', ['crates/cambium/cambium-genet-winit-host/tests','crates/cambium/cambium-genet-winit-host/src/occlusion_tests.rs'], 'Synthetic delayed pixels are accurately labeled as pairing mechanics; scenario tests explicitly fail lost captures, failed acceptance and completion errors. Geometry tests exercise actual retained layout but selected font/system assumptions and stale prose remain bounded. This pass read all 48 native-host files, not run the full native integration suite.')
]
